<https://graphdb.example.com/resource/places/GML_4A96E6DF-73E8-48C3-BBE3-0F5B55E81166> a xp:Regulation ;
    gml:id "GML_4A96E6DF-73E8-48C3-BBE3-0F5B55E81166" ;
    xp:key "4.3" ;
    xp:plan <https://graphdb.example.com/resource/places/GML_c1979111-6f94-4f90-a7ad-d8061446d21e> ;
    xp:text "For protection against traffic noise, in the building areas - WA 4 along the line E2 - E1 - E10 - E9 - WA 5 along the line F2 - F1 - F9 - F8 - WA 7 along the line H3 - H1 - H9 - H8 - WA 8 along the line I2 - I1 - I11 - I10 - WA 9 along the line J2 - J1 - J10 - J9 Exterior living areas structurally connected to buildings (e.g. loggias, balconies, terraces) are only permitted as glazed porches or glazed loggias. Exempt from the regulation are apartments that have at least one structurally connected outdoor living area that faces away from the aforementioned lines. In the case of dwellings with several structurally connected outdoor living areas that face only the aforementioned lines, at least one structurally connected outdoor living area must be constructed as a glazed porch or glazed loggia in each case." .

