<https://graphdb.example.com/resource/places/GML_65B4D81D-F2F0-45C0-91B4-ECB8B3DB5605> a xp:Regulation ;
    gml:id "GML_65B4D81D-F2F0-45C0-91B4-ECB8B3DB5605" ;
    xp:key "1.2" ;
    xp:plan <https://graphdb.example.com/resource/places/GML_c1979111-6f94-4f90-a7ad-d8061446d21e> ;
    xp:text "The other special area for the purpose of \"MOBILITY HUB AND RETAIL\" serves primarily serves the parking of vehicles, area logistics and local supply. The following are permitted 1.2.1. large garages for the needs caused by the use permitted in the general residential areas and the other special area are permitted; 1.2.2. storage facilities serving the supply of the plan area, waste collection areas, bicycle parking and facilities for the handling and storage of courier, express and parcel consignments, express and parcel deliveries; 1.2.3. on the first full storey, food stores with an operational sales area of no more than 1,200 m². The sales area for centre-relevant local supply (food, beverages and tobacco products, medicines, medical, orthopaedic and cosmetic articles, detergents, cleaning agents, etc.), medicines, medical, orthopaedic and cosmetic articles, detergents and cleaning agents, books, magazines, newspapers, stationery and office requisites stationery, office supplies) may not fall below 90% of the total sales area. of the total sales area; 1.2.4. Shops, pubs and restaurants serving the needs of the planned area, as well as non-interfering craft businesses; 1.2.5. Facilities for religious, cultural, social, health and sporting purposes serving the area covered by the plan, social, health and sporting purposes; 1.2.6. Rooms for the professional practice of freelancers and such tradesmen, who exercise their profession in a similar manner; 1.2.7. Landing sites for parcel and logistics drones and other comparable unmanned drones and other comparable unmanned aerial vehicles suitable and intended for the ransport of goods and merchandise." .

<https://graphdb.example.com/resource/places/GML_66767E4C-EDA3-445A-9ECD-C7DA7F747AE0> a xp:Regulation ;
    gml:id "GML_66767E4C-EDA3-445A-9ECD-C7DA7F747AE0" ;
    xp:key "5.3" ;
    xp:plan <https://graphdb.example.com/resource/places/GML_c1979111-6f94-4f90-a7ad-d8061446d21e> ;
    xp:text "In the building areas and in the other special area, at least 30 % of the closed exterior wall areas are to be landscaped. The plantings are to be maintained and replanted if they are lost. Along lines E1 - E10, F1 - F9, H1 - H9, I1 - I11, and J1 - J10, at least 30% of the exterior wall areas shall be landscaped. The plantings may be counted towards the greening requirements of sentence 1. The plantings must be maintained and replaced if they are lost." .

<https://graphdb.example.com/resource/places/GML_68A8123D-EAD2-4DB3-B8DF-36F1BB0853E1> a xp:Regulation ;
    gml:id "GML_68A8123D-EAD2-4DB3-B8DF-36F1BB0853E1" ;
    xp:key "3.3" ;
    xp:plan <https://graphdb.example.com/resource/places/GML_c1979111-6f94-4f90-a7ad-d8061446d21e> ;
    xp:text "In the building areas, only residential buildings may be erected in which a share of at least 30 % of the permissible floor area could be subsidized with funds from the social housing promotion funds. As an exception, residential buildings without apartments eligible for subsidies may be permitted may be permitted as an exception if the minimum proportion required in accordance with Sentence 1 is building in the area covered by the development plan." .

<https://graphdb.example.com/resource/places/GML_6BAAD202-17D2-465D-87A4-9BD8541FFC70> a xp:Regulation ;
    gml:id "GML_6BAAD202-17D2-465D-87A4-9BD8541FFC70" ;
    xp:key "4.1" ;
    xp:plan <https://graphdb.example.com/resource/places/GML_c1979111-6f94-4f90-a7ad-d8061446d21e> ;
    xp:text "For protection against traffic noise, buildings in the building areas must have - WA 4 along the line E1 - E10 - WA 5 along the line F1 - F9 - WA 7 along the line H2 - H1 - H9 - H8 - WA 8 along the line I2 - I1 - I11 - WA 9 along the line J1 - J10 - J9 in apartments - with one or two living rooms at least one living room, - with more than two rooms, at least half of the rooms. recreation rooms with at least one window facing away from the above-mentioned lines. Exempt from the regulation are apartments on block corners in the general residential areas WA7 to WA9, where at least two exterior walls are oriented to the above-mentioned lines." .

