<https://graphdb.example.com/resource/places/GML_BE2E8B37-2A73-40F0-9282-ECFCEDB51B99> a xp:Regulation ;
    gml:id "GML_BE2E8B37-2A73-40F0-9282-ECFCEDB51B99" ;
    xp:key "5.9" ;
    xp:plan <https://graphdb.example.com/resource/places/GML_c1979111-6f94-4f90-a7ad-d8061446d21e> ;
    xp:text "In the general residential areas, the non-buildable property areas between the traffic area and the building boundary or building line (front garden areas) are to be enclosed along the traffic area with a 50 cm high wall. Otherwise, only access roads to the building and parking spaces for bicycles can be permitted in the front garden areas. Along the lines B1 - B2 - B3, C4 - C5, G2 - G3, I7 - I8 and J4 - J5, plaza areas may also be permitted. The front yard areas are otherwise to be landscaped with perennials and shrubs. The plantings are to be maintained and replaced if they are lost." .

<https://graphdb.example.com/resource/places/GML_C3009273-7674-4653-BE9C-EA45A708C116> a xp:Regulation ;
    gml:id "GML_C3009273-7674-4653-BE9C-EA45A708C116" ;
    xp:key "5.1" ;
    xp:plan <https://graphdb.example.com/resource/places/GML_c1979111-6f94-4f90-a7ad-d8061446d21e> ;
    xp:text "In the building areas, at least 40% of the roof surfaces are to be extensively greened with herbs and grasses. Roof surfaces of ancillary facilities within the meaning of § 14 of the German Land Use Ordinance (Baunutzungsverordnung) are not included in this figure. The rootable part of the roof structure must be at least 10 cm. The plantings are to be maintained and replaced if they are lost. In addition, at least 40% of the roof areas in the construction areas are to be laid out as biodiversity roofs. Roof areas of ancillary facilities within the meaning of § 14 of the Building Use Ordinance are not to be included in this calculation. The biodiversity roof is simply to be intensively greened. The rootable part of the roof structure must be at least 15 cm. To ensure biodiversity in the sense of the biodiversity roof, the rootable part of the roof structure must be at least 80 cm on at least 10% of the area of the biodiversity roof. For every 10.0 m² or part thereof of the biodiversity roof, at least one biotope element must be installed. Biotope elements within the meaning of the stipulation are deadwood elements, stone elements, damp depressions and nesting aids for insects. At least 50% of the biotope elements must be deadwood elements. The plantings are to be maintained and replanted if they are lost. In order to ensure biodiversity, other measures of equal effect may be taken as an exception. The stipulation for the installation as a biodiversity roof does not apply to roof areas of high-rise buildings. These roof surfaces must be extensively greened to at least 80% in accordance with sentences 1 to 4" .

<https://graphdb.example.com/resource/places/GML_C9F47915-60F6-4035-9032-E6E40BE571C8> a xp:DeterminationAccordingToStateLaw ;
    geo:hasDefaultGeometry <https://graphdb.example.com/resource/places/GML_C9F47915-60F6-4035-9032-E6E40BE571C8/geo> ;
